<title>UK: East Midland Elec announces board changes.</title>
<headline>East Midland Elec announces board changes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>East Midland Electricity said on Tuesday that non-executives Sir Nigel Rudd, Gareth Cooper, Nicholas Corah, Alan Schroeder and David Thompson had resigned from the board of directors.</p>
<p>Rudd and Corah have also stepped down as chairman and deputy chairman respectively.</p>
<p>They will be replaced on the board by Thomas Capps, Thomas Chewning, David Heavenridge, Thomas Farrell II, Linwood Robertson and William Thomas who were nominated by East Midland's new parent company Dominion Resources.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
